\newlabel{fig:transverserelaxation}{{3.6}{21}{Evolution of $\langle S_{xy}\rangle (t)$. The transverse component of the nuclear spin relaxes toward the equilibrium state, leading to the loss of information. The relaxation rate is characterized by a time constant: \(T_2\)}{figure.caption.18}{}}
\newlabel{fig:bloch_transverse}{{\caption@xref {fig:bloch_transverse}{ on input line 809}}{21}{Transverse Relaxation}{figure.caption.19}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.7}{\ignorespaces Bloch sphere representation of Transverse relaxation. The transverse component of the nuclear spin relaxes from an example superposition state \(\frac  {1}{\sqrt  {2}}(|0\rangle + |1\rangle )\), toward the equilibrium maximum mixed state, losing phase information and coherence. The precession around the external magnetic field continues at the Larmor frequency.}}{21}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
