\newlabel{fig:hardpulse_example}{{4.1}{28}{The example Euler angle rotation shown previously in Figure~\ref {fig:RxRyRx} can be implemented using only maximum amplitude hard pulses. The $R_x(\pi /2)$ rotation is a 40~\textmu s pulse with phase $0^\circ $, the $R_y(\pi )$ rotation is an 80~\textmu s pulse with phase $90^\circ $, and the final $R_x(-\pi /2)$ rotation is a 40~\textmu s pulse with phase $180^\circ $}{figure.caption.24}{}}
